@vineelbhat Following up on the comment above: could you please rebase onto current main and drop the indexer/Engram changes already covered by #41659?

Please also rerun the benchmarks against that updated main, using the same hardware, server flags, and workloads for both arms, and update the PR description with the baseline/head commit SHAs, remaining host-sync counts, prefill/TTFT and serving results, and a GSM8K accuracy check. The current numbers include optimizations that have already landed, so we need to measure the incremental benefit of the remaining changes.

Please keep the mHC `record_stream` removal in a separate PR so its stream-ordering and tensor-lifetime assumptions can be reviewed independently. Thanks!

